    {
      "id": "2122433533079695721",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2103567689515954176/aR-Kjpp4_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T20:56:01.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-17 04:56:01",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "We've all read about Elon's working style being different. Hands-on, to say the least. Here's my anecdotal Elon moment: in 2014, we were raising capital and got introduced to John Doerr through our friend Jerry Murdock, and John wanted to meet me and Nami in Sicily, where they had a private event. During the evening, we jumped on a small bus together with Elon to join a dinner. At that time, Tesla had just opened their first showroom in Sweden, Täby. I told Elon that I booked a test ride with their new Model S but was wondering why they had a two-month waiting time to try the car. He was shocked/frustrated about the waiting time. He picked up his phone, made a call and sent some messages. The next week, Tesla Sweden called me and said, \"Hi, you signed up for the test drive. We just got many more demo cars delivered and you can come and try it today already.\" That's how you get shit done! Can't even imagine how he operates today, but I'm sure it's still in the details and solving problems. That was inspiring, to say the least.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "AlanMamedi",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1707789769730592768/t2kK7-gj_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-16 22:43:32",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-16T14:43:32.000Z",
        "id": "2122339794113953836",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "Alan Mamedi",
        "text": "We've all read about Elon's working style being different. Hands-on, to say the least. Here's my anecdotal Elon moment: in 2014, we were raising capital and got introduced to John Doerr through our friend Jerry Murdock, and John wanted to meet me and Nami in Sicily, where they had a private event. During the evening, we jumped on a small bus together with Elon to join a dinner. At that time, Tesla had just opened their first showroom in Sweden, Täby. I told Elon that I booked a test ride with their new Model S but was wondering why they had a two-month waiting time to try the car. He was shocked/frustrated about the waiting time. He picked up his phone, made a call and sent some messages. The next week, Tesla Sweden called me and said, \"Hi, you signed up for the test drive. We just got many more demo cars delivered and you can come and try it today already.\" That's how you get shit done! Can't even imagine how he operates today, but I'm sure it's still in the details and solving problems. That was inspiring, to say the least.",
